name "sub:The-Installer-NSIS"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Nullsoft Scriptable Install System (NSIS) is a script based Installer for
 Windows 
\shape italic
to create the logic to handle even the most complex installation tasks
\shape default
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "nsis-main-page"

\end_inset

.
 It was developed by Nullsoft.
 NSIS is open source software and licensed under different free software
 licences 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "nsis-main-page"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It has no graphical user interface, so for a more comfortable development
 we used the HM NIS Editor 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "hm-nsis-editor-homepage"

\end_inset

.
 Using this Editor, or the corresponding command from the command line (as
 shown in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Compile-the-package-NSIS"

\end_inset

), the NSIS scripts can be compiled to create the executable installer packages.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The advantages of NSIS are its wide spreading and that it is freely available.
 Its biggest competitor is the Windows Installer (MSI), which is a proprietary
 system by Microsoft.
 Due to Microsoft's version compatibility policy, different installers for
 different Windows versions would be required 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "msi-msdn-homepage"

\end_inset

.
 Because of this issue and its closed-source principle we decided to use
 NSIS instead.
\end_layout

