\begin_layout Standard
Besides the 
\family typewriter
DEBIAN
\family default
 folder with package information, the root folder also contains the files
 that have to be installed to the file system of the target system.
 These files are organized in a directory structure that represents the
 target system.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For example, if a file called 
\family typewriter
info.txt
\family default
 has to be installed to the
\family typewriter
 /opt
\family default
 folder of the file system, simply a folder called 
\family typewriter
opt
\family default
 has to be created inside the root folder and the 
\family typewriter
info.txt
\family default
 file has to be put in there.
 While installing, the 
\family typewriter
opt
\family default
 folder in the root of the target file system will be created if it doesn’t
 exist and the text file will be copied there 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "deb-basic-package-howto"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Following this easy example we created an 
\family typewriter
opt
\family default
 folder and put the BSF4ooRexx install folder in it.
 During installation this folder will be copied into the 
\family typewriter
opt
\family default
 directory of the target system.
 From there we will be able to execute the installation scripts (which is
 described in more detail in the following chapter), that configure BSF4ooRexx
 for the target system.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Install scripts 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sub:Install-scripts-DEB"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The file system structure is, as defined in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:File-system-structure-DEB"

\end_inset

, a vital part of the installation package but its abilities are limited
 to simple copy-and-paste operations.
 In order to add some logic to the package and make it more intelligent,
 it is possible to define up to four scripts with predefined names that
 are executed on special conditions 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "deb-package-basics,deb-maintainer-guide"

\end_inset

:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
preinst
\family default
 – This script defines operations that have to occur before the contents
 of the package are copied and the 
\family typewriter
postinst
\family default
 script is executed.
 This could be to stop a specific service or create a user etc.
 We use this script to remove old versions of BSF4ooRexx from the 
\family typewriter
/opt
\family default
 directory.
 The complete source code of the script is depicted in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Debian-Package-preinst-Script"

\end_inset

 in the Appendix.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
postinst
\family default
 – Operations within this script are executed after the package’s contents
 have been copied to their destination in the file system.
 Typical operations could be the restart of a service or the configuration
 of system-specific settings.
 In our case, we use the 
\family typewriter
postinst
\family default
 script to run the 
\family typewriter
setupAllAndRun.rex
\family default
 script from the BSF4ooRexx distribution to set up all required components.
 The script is shown in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Debian-Package-postinst-Script"

\end_inset

 in the Appendix.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
prerm
\family default
 – As the name indicates, the 
\family typewriter
prerm
\family default
-script contains commands that are executed before the package is removed.
 We used it to remove all BSF4ooRexx files from the file system before the
 package itself is removed.
 The content of the postrm script is shown in chapter 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Debian-Package-prerm-Script"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
postrm
\family default
 – This script contains commands that are executed after the package has
 been removed from the system.
 Typically, such commands restart a service, remove a user or clean up temporary
 data.
 This script type is not used in the package.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Please note that the scripts must use these predefined names.
 If they do not, the package will not work as intended.
