\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Stages and their functions, as described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "rpm-full-howto-build-a-package"

\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "tab:Stages-and-their-functions-RPM"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As one can see from this definition, the system primarily aims at creating
 packages directly from the source code.
 Normally, the source code in unpacked, configured, compiled, tested and
 installed inside the buildroot directory.
 Based upon that the package is built, containing the required files only.
 In our case it is not really necessary to compile any source code.
 Therefore, the 
\family typewriter
%build
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
%check
\family default
 stages, for example, are not used.
 
\family typewriter
%check
\family default
 is not even listed in listing 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "src_bsf4oorexx_spec_RPM"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
During the preparation stage, as already mentioned, the BSF4ooRexx distribution
 file is unpacked to the build directory using the 
\family typewriter
unzip
\family default
 command.
 Because we don't need to compile any files, the 
\family typewriter
%build
\family default
 stage does not contain any commands.
 Reaching the 
\family typewriter
%install
\family default
 stage, the buildroot directory is cleaned and freshly populated with a
 
\family typewriter
tmp
\family default
 directory and the unpacked BSF4ooRexx files.
 This is necessary, because the contents of the BSF4ooRexx distribution
 will be placed in the systems 
\family typewriter
/tmp
\family default
 directory during installation.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The last two important settings are 
\family typewriter
%post
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
%preun
\family default
.
 The first one, 
\family typewriter
%post
\family default
, allows the definition of commands that will be executed, after the package
 has been installed and the files have been moved to the filesystem.
 In our case, an existing (old) BSF4ooRexx directory under 
\family typewriter
/opt
\family default
 will here be removed, the BSF4ooRexx install folder contained in the package
 is moved to
\family typewriter
 /tmp
\family default
 and the according setup script is started.
 After this step is complete, BSF4ooRexx is installed and fully functional.
 Just like in case of the Debian package, there are no separate RPM packages
 for 32 and 64 bit installations required, because the BSF4ooRexx distribution's
 install scripts are used here, which can handle both situations.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The second setting, 
\family typewriter
%preun
\family default
, is used, when before the package is uninstalled.
 It runs the uninstall script that comes with BSF4ooRexx, which removes
 all settings and files that have been made or created during installation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
After these settings have been configured successfully, the package can
 finally be built.
 
\end_layout

